    "AiFallbackReason": {
      "description": "Why a failed provider request is a candidate for retry on another model.\n\nSet on AiProviderRequestError by each engine from the provider's own error\ncodes, since an HTTP status alone does not separate a rate limit from an\nexhausted quota. Errors that a different model would not fix (validation,\na content refusal) carry no reason. Account-level\nfailures (a rejected key, a spend cap) do carry one: a candidate on\nanother provider uses another account.\n\nMembers:\n    UNAVAILABLE: The provider or model cannot serve right now: 5xx,\n        overloaded, model not ready, or the connection failed.\n    RATE_LIMITED: A transient 429; the engine's own backoff runs first.\n    QUOTA_EXHAUSTED: Billing, credit, quota, or a spend cap is used up,\n        so retrying the same model is pointless.\n    AUTH_REJECTED: The provider rejected the credentials or the account\n        (401/403, an invalid or expired key, a disabled organization).\n        Retrying the same provider is pointless; another provider's\n        account can still serve.\n    TIMEOUT: The caller's own deadline passed before the provider\n        answered. Off by default in the fallback layer: the deadline is\n        a caller setting, and failing over adds the next candidate's\n        wait on top of it. A caller with a short deadline turns it on\n        to treat a hung provider as an outage.\n    MODEL_UNAVAILABLE: The model id is unknown, retired, or not offered\n        in the configured region. Usually a configuration error, so a\n        fallback layer should not act on it unless told to.\n    INVALID_OUTPUT: The model answered a structured request, and was\n        billed for it, but the answer is not valid JSON, not a JSON\n        object, or fails the response model. Off by default: a bad\n        answer then costs a second billed call on another model, which\n        is a spending decision. Turn it on to let the chain try the next\n        model and the router escalate on bad output; each discarded\n        answer is a wasted line item on the request's cost report.",
      "enum": [
        "unavailable",
        "rate_limited",
        "quota_exhausted",
        "model_unavailable",
        "auth_rejected",
        "timeout",
        "invalid_output"
      ],
      "title": "AiFallbackReason",
      "type": "string"
    },
